    -------- DEFERRAL EVIDENCE (captured, not asserted) --------
    Both app schemes run a mandatory pre-build action that assembles the KMP core as
    Frameworks/Shared.xcframework via Gradle (Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh, ADR-004).
    The iOS build was launched and left running; as of 01:38:01 (~16 min after launch):
      - iOS xcodebuild  : still-running, output buffered (0 lines emitted)
      - Shared.xcframework : absent
      - slot-77 Gradle  : never scheduled (no slot-77/apps/shared gradlew process)
      - peer Kotlin builds running concurrently across sibling parallel slots: 3
    A single shared Gradle daemon (GRADLE_USER_HOME=~/.gradle) is being monopolized by 4-6
    peer slots all running :core:assembleSharedXCFramework simultaneously; this slot's
    pre-action is starved and never reaches the Swift compile phase. This is environment/
    cross-slot resource contention for an out-of-scope dependency framework, not a fault in
    the WeekOverWeekSummary surface. macOS shares the identical Shared.xcframework prerequisite
    (and the documented macOS code-signing requirement); it was not launched separately so as
    not to compound the shared-daemon contention. The surface contains NO platform-conditional
    (#if os) code, so the gate [5] full type-check result applies verbatim to both app targets.

    This is the same disposition accepted for the sibling surfaces in this slot:
    p4-apple-feature-views-0077-SummaryHeroCards.log (IOS_EXIT/MAC_EXIT deferred, EXIT=0/DONE)
    and p4-apple-feature-views-0079-WeekSelector.log.

